WS73 production codec fuzz (offline C, not a kernel/USB test)
==========================================================

From the Linux checkout, with Clang/libFuzzer, ASAN/UBSAN, matching llvm-profdata,
llvm-cov and nm installed:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/fuzz/test_ws73_codec_verdict.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/run_ws73_codec_fuzz.py \
      --output /tmp/ws73-codec-fuzz-new-run --runs 20000 --seed 730111

The output directory must not exist. CC, LLVM_PROFDATA and LLVM_COV select the
recorded tools. The runner links unchanged drivers/sparklink/ws73/wire.c and
dli.c; it does not load kernel code, install services, read firmware or open USB.
Host execution here is a pure-code exception to VM-only driver/device testing.
Never send fuzzer inputs to real WS73 hardware.

The fixed public-format corpus has no captures/SDK/firmware/keys. It covers empty
and truncated input, relay/link/encryption events, ACB/PB,253/254/255/2047 lengths,
20KiB RX budget, aggregate slots and a malformed later slot. Short exploration
extends its own copy; preserve both corpus directories, the seed, crashes, logs,
binary, coverage profiles/export and report.json. Minimize confirmed failures and
turn them into fixed production regressions; reruns never erase originals.

The harness uses real parser/encoder bodies, libc allocation, and an observer
callback checking input bounds/routing plus an explicit ECANCELED alternative.
It checks failed aggregate validation exposes no earlier valid slot, output
capacity and failure atomicity, complete ACB roundtrips, and fresh valid parser
reentry after arbitrary input. It intentionally does not pass invalid C pointers.
EFAULT/bad user pointers belong to the actual syscall VM gate.

The runner checks sanitizer/coverage symbols, full libFuzzer terminal summaries,
actual execution counts of required production functions and unchanged source
hashes. Missing tools/results/profiles, sanitizer diagnostics, a masked failure
or truncated logs cannot pass. Synthetic supervisor negative-control tests
are separate from production codec exploration. The initial unqualified receipt
precedes Git/source/tool metadata collection; each external metadata command has
a recorded30-second wall deadline. A metadata timeout is a failed/unverified run,
never permission to omit source identity or upgrade an older run. The supervisor
terminates its own timed-out command group, including inherited-pipe Git helpers;
this does not authorize killing other builds. Preserve partial logs and report.

BOUNDED_FUZZ_COMPLETED_NO_FINDING means only the recorded finite input budget.
It is not a proof or a kernel KASAN/KCSAN/lockdep qualification. Query/BSLE state
machines, stream split/reassembly, allocation failure, Session/Grant/credit,
USB/callback/locks, security, real air traffic and hardware recovery remain in
separate selftests/formal/VM gates. LSan under ptrace may fail in a restricted
sandbox; retain that tool failure and rerun in an authorized ordinary process,
without disabling the detector or treating DONE alone as success.

Dynamic basic CMTC codec uses the same fail-closed supervisor (not a second
protocol Engine):

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/run_ws73_codec_fuzz.py \
      --contract cmtc --output /tmp/sparklink-cmtc-fuzz-new-run \
      --runs 20000 --seed 730111

This variant links actual sle_channel_wire.c and channel/signal_fuzz.c, keeps
hand-authored seeds in channel/signal_corpus.json, bounds input to64 bytes, and
requires both actual signaling decoder and encoder to execute. It checks decode
failure atomicity and exact legal roundtrip bytes/fields. It does not prove
Runtime credit, Session/Grant lifecycle, concurrency, firmware or peer delivery.
The fixed channel codec and WS73 transport targets retain their own coverage.
